{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/review-analyzer","name":"review-analyzer","description":"Drop in product reviews to get aspect-level sentiment, trend lines, suspicious-review detection, and an AI executive summary with reply drafts.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T04:30:44Z","updated":"2026-10-10T03:51:09Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/review-analyzer/","topics":["github-pages","javascript","nlp","reviews","sentiment-analysis"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/review-analyzer/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.242Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.242Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.242Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.242Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Drop in product reviews to get aspect-level sentiment, trend lines, suspicious-review detection, and an AI executive summary with reply drafts.","Review Radar reads hundreds of reviews so you don't have to. A local NLP pipeline splits reviews into sentences and scores sentiment with a lexicon that handles negation, intensifiers and 'but' clauses. It maps each sentence to product aspects (sound, battery, fit, connectivity …) to build a diverging aspect-sentiment chart, and plots rating and text sentiment month by month. Weighted log-odds with an informative prior surfaces the words that separate 5from 1reviews. Suspicious-review heuristics catch near-duplicates (shingle Jaccard), same-day 5bursts, generic one-liners and rating/text…"],"features":["CSV import with auto column detection, paste mode, and a 146-review synthetic sample with real trends","Sentence-level lexicon sentiment with negation scope, intensifiers and contrastive 'but' weighting","Aspect extraction + diverging positive/neutral/negative bars (click to filter)","Monthly rating vs text-sentimen